    "content_text": "Altmark Lithium Extraction (ALE) project: Evonik Catalysts supports Pilot Phase II\nEvonik Catalysts is supporting the next phase of Neptune Energy's Altmark Lithium Extraction Project (ALE) in northern Germany\nEvonik Catalysts Liocel® adsorbent selected for test phase of Neptune Energy's Altmark Lithium Extraction Project\nMaterials successful preliminary testing will now be evaluated in a pilot plant by Fraunhofer IEG\nOn-site application and process know-how supporting Pilot Phase II with Fraunhofer IEG\nHanau, Germany. Evonik Catalysts is supporting the next phase of Neptune Energy's Altmark Lithium Extraction Project (ALE) in northern Germany. Following the successful preliminary testing, Evonik's Liocel® adsorbent has been selected as the first material to be evaluated in the direct lithium extraction (DLE) pilot plant developed by Fraunhofer IEG.\nThe Altmark region in Saxony-Anhalt contains a project-specific lithium resource estimated at 43 million tonnes of lithium carbonate equivalent (LCE). Neptune Energy plans to extract lithium from geothermal brine using DLE technology as part of its ambition to contribute to a resilient European supply of critical raw materials.\nDuring Pilot Phase I, Neptune evaluated several commercially available DLE technologies under Altmark-specific conditions, including ion-exchange and adsorption processes. Based on these evaluations, adsorption technology was selected for further investigation in Pilot Phase II.\nFor this test phase, Evonik has been selected to provide its Liocel® adsorbent following its demonstrated stability and strong performance in preliminary testing. In addition, Evonik is supporting the pilot program with application and process know-how on-site.\nThe pilot plant developed by Fraunhofer IEG enables oxygen-free lithium extraction and can process up to 1,000 liters of geothermal brine per day. In pilot phase II, Neptune Energy will test various adsorbent materials and be assessed over the coming months to support the selection of an optimal solution for potential future industrial-scale deployment.\n\"We are pleased to partner with Neptune Energy and Frauenhofer IEG in this important next phase of the project,\" said Michael Frey, Vice President and Head of Process Catalysts & Adsorbents at Evonik.\n\"Together, we look forward to further evaluating adsorption-based lithium extraction under the specific conditions of the Altmark resource and contributing our technical expertise to the project.\"\nEvonik: Leading beyond chemistry\nEvonik goes beyond the boundaries of chemistry with its combination of innovative strength and leading technological expertise. The global chemical company, headquartered in Essen, Germany, is active in more than 100 countries and generated sales of €14.1 billion and earnings (adjusted EBITDA) of €1.9 billion in 2025. The common motivation of the approximately 31,000 employees: to provide customers with a decisive competitive advantage with tailor-made products and solutions as a superforce for industry, thereby improving people's lives. In all markets. Every day.\nAbout Custom Solutions \nThe Custom Solutions segment focuses on innovation-driven, tailor-made solutions for customers in specific growth markets. These solutions include additives for coatings, adhesives and sealants, polyurethane foams and lubricants, catalysts, and ingredients for the cosmetics, cleaning and pharmaceutical industries. In 2025, the segment generated sales of €5.4 billion with around 9,500 employees. \nDisclaimer\nIn so far as forecasts or expectations are expressed in this release or where our statements concern the future, these forecasts, expectations or statements may involve known or unknown risks and uncertainties. Actual results or developments may vary, depending on changes in the operating environment. Neither Evonik Industries AG nor its group companies assume an obligation to update the forecasts, expectations or statements contained in this release.\nEvonik Industries AG\nOpernplatz 1\n45128 Essen\nGermany\nPhone +49 201 177-01\nwww.evonik.com\nSupervisory Board Bernd Tönjes, Chairman Executive Board Christian Kullmann, Lauren Kjeldsen, Dr. Claudine Mollenkopf, Michael Rauch, Deputy Chairman Dr. Claus Rettig, Thomas Wessel\nRegistered Office is Essen Register Court Essen Local Court Commercial Registry B 19474\nOnline version press release",
