    "content_text": "For Immediate Release\nCompany Name:\nRepresentative:\nSecurities Code:\nStock Exchange\nListings:\nInquiries:\nAugust 12, 2026\nSumitomo Chemical Co., Ltd.\nNobuaki Mito\nRepresentative Director & President\n4005\nTokyo Stock Exchange Prime Market\nShoko Wato\nGeneral Manager\nCorporate Communications Dept.\n(Tel: +81-3-5201-0200)\nAnnouncement Regarding Report on the Group\nSumitomo Chemical Co., Ltd. hereby announces that its subsidiary, Sumitomo Pharma Co., Ltd.,\ntoday issued a statement entitled “Regarding a Report Concerning Sumitomo Pharma (The\nCompany's Views on ‘Sumitomo Chemical and Sumitomo Pharmaceutical: Part II - CiRA, Dr.\nYamanaka, and the undisclosed history of image duplication concerns’).” For further details,\nplease see the attachment.\nAugust 12, 2026\nSumitomo Pharma Co., Ltd.\nRegarding a Report Concerning Sumitomo Pharma (The Company's Views on\n“Sumitomo Chemical and Sumitomo Pharmaceutical: Part II - CiRA,\nDr. Yamanaka, and the undisclosed history of image duplication concerns”)\nSumitomo Pharma Co., Ltd. (Head Office: Osaka, Japan; Representative Director, President and\nCEO: Toru Kimura; the “Company”) has confirmed that Gotham City Research LLC (“GCR”)\npublished a report, “Sumitomo Chemical and Sumitomo Pharmaceutical: Part II - CiRA, Dr.\nYamanaka, and the undisclosed history of image duplication concerns” (the “August 7 Report”),\nconcerning the Company on August 7, 2026.\nThe August 7 Report is based on GCR’s unilateral views and assertions, which are not acceptable\nto the Company. In addition, GCR discloses in the August 7 Report that it and its partner companies\nand related persons “hold short positions in the covered issuers’ stock and stand to profit in the\nevent the covered issuer’s stock price declines.”\nThe August 7 Report contains statements regarding AMCHEPRY®, one of the Company's products.\nAMCHEPRY® has been developed through many years of industry-academia-government\ncollaboration with Kyoto University and other institutions. The Company has confirmed the reliability\nof the materials submitted for regulatory review of AMCHEPRY®, and AMCHEPRY® was granted\nconditional and time-limited approval following scientific and medical review and assessment by\nthe relevant regulatory authorities.\nIn addition, in accordance with the conditions attached to the approval, the Company is\nappropriately conducting a post-marketing clinical study (Phase 4 study) and steadily accumulating\nfurther evidence regarding the efficacy and safety of AMCHEPRY®, with the aim of obtaining full\napproval as early as possible.\nThe Company will continue to provide timely and appropriate disclosures to its shareholders and\ninvestors.\nThe Company also notes that GCR published a report on August 3, 2026, containing unilateral\nviews regarding the Company’s financial reporting. The Company will take appropriate action,\nincluding legal action where necessary, in response to inaccurate or misleading information in order\nto protect the interests of the Company and its shareholders and investors.\nContact:\nCorporate Communications, Sumitomo Pharma Co., Ltd.\nE-mail: prir@sumitomo-pharma.co.jp",
