    "content_text": "1-9-2, Higashi-Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo 105-8640 JAPAN\nTel : +81-3-6218-3500 Fax : +81-3-6218-3682\nhttp://www.jsr.co.jp\nFY2025 Full-Year Business Status Briefing\nBriefing materials:\nFiscal Year Ending March 31 2026 Business Status Briefing Materials\nP4 FY2025 Full-Year Results\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFY2025 full-year results. Revenue was 440.7 billion yen, an increase of 51.9 billion yen\nYoY. Core operating profit was 62.3 billion yen, an increase of 64.0 billion yen YoY. Net\nprofit was 60.7 billion yen, an increase of 278.4 billion yen YoY.\nBoth revenue and profit increased significantly YoY, and core operating profit exceeded\nthe previous record high posted in FY2007. Net profit also reached a record high.\nProfitability improved, driven by growth in EM. At the same time, LS business\ndivestitures and other restructuring measures progressed, and borrowings were reduced,\nresulting in an improved financial position. As a result, the company recovered sharply\nfrom the prior-year loss caused by impairment losses and other factors.\nIn EM, customer adoption progressed across product categories, including advanced\nlithography materials, process materials and packaging materials, driving revenue growth.\nIn DIS/OPT, adoption expanded not only in new materials for LCD and OLED but also\nin optical film applications in OPT, including ARTON resin and NIR cut filters.\nIn PLA, sales volumes declined due to weak demand in automotive and industrial\napplications. Although, the company worked to improve spreads and promoted\nexpansion into higher-value-added areas.\nIn LS, the business remained in the midst of structural reform, including efforts to\nimprove profitability and business transfers. As these measures progressed, the\nturnaround of the CDMO business, which had faced operational challenges, also\nadvanced and was completed.\nP5 Revenue Trend\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEM achieved 24% revenue growth YoY, supported by strong demand in advanced\nsemiconductor applications. Revenue reached a record high.\nDIS came in largely in line with the previous fiscal year, excluding temporary license\nincome recorded in the prior year.\nOPT continued to expand steadily, including in optical filter applications.\nPLA declined slightly.\nLS improved substantially as the turnaround of the CDMO business progressed.\nAs a result, FY2025 revenue came in at 440.7 billion yen, up 13% YoY, driven by strong\n1\n1-9-2, Higashi-Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo 105-8640 JAPAN\nTel : +81-3-6218-3500 Fax : +81-3-6218-3682\nhttp://www.jsr.co.jp\ngrowth in EM and improved profitability in LS.\nP6 Core Operating Profit and Net Profit\n Growth in DS, including EM, and LS’s return to profitability drove core operating profit\nto 62.3 billion yen.\n In addition to the improvement in core operating profit, profit reached 60.7 billion yen,\nby gains from LS-related divestiture and the absence of impairment losses recorded in\nFY2024. This represented a sharp recovery from the FY2024 trough and a new record\nhigh.\nP7 FY2025 Full-Year Results\n\n\n\n\n\nOn a consolidated basis, growth in DS and improvement in LS drove each profit line back\ninto positive territory, while core operating profit and net profit reached record highs.\nIn DS, EM achieved 24% revenue growth, driven by advanced applications and other\nareas. As a result, the segment also posted record-high revenue and profit.\nIn PLA, revenue declined slightly, but profit exceeded the previous year.\nIn LS, core operating profit turned positive. This reflected the results of business\nstructural reform.\nUnder IFRS, divested businesses are classified as discontinued operations, and only\nprofit from discontinued operations is separately presented. On this page, a separate\ncolumn for discontinued operations adjustments has been provided to deduct the\nrevenue and core operating profit of the IVD and BPM businesses, for which divestitures\nhave been completed.\nP8 Statements of Income (PL)\n In FY2024, results showed a substantial loss, reflecting impairment losses recorded in\nother operating expenses, a temporary increase in expenses associated with becoming an\nunlisted company, and a temporary decline in revenue in LS. In FY2025, however,\nperformance improved significantly, driven by strong revenue growth in EM and\nimprovement in LS.\n Operating profit for FY2025 on the consolidated statement of profit was 40.5 billion yen.\nThe difference from the core operating profit of 62.3 billion yen shown on the previous\npage is attributable to PPA amortization and non-core expenses related to business\ntransfers and structural reform.\n Profit consisted of 1.8 billion yen from continuing operations and 58.9 billion yen from\ndiscontinued operations, mainly gains from business transfers. The above-mentioned\n2\n1-9-2, Higashi-Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo 105-8640 JAPAN\nTel : +81-3-6218-3500 Fax : +81-3-6218-3682\nhttp://www.jsr.co.jp\nPPA amortization and non-core expenses are all related to continuing operations.\nP9 Statement of Financial Position (BS)\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCash and cash equivalents increased by 30.0 billion yen YoY.\nWithin non-current assets, goodwill and other intangible assets declined due to business\ndivestitures and PPA amortization.\nLiabilities decreased by 40.3 billion yen with borrowings declined on both a current and\nnon-current basis.\nEquity increased by 69.3 billion yen, driven by a substantial return to profitability.\nNet debt decreased by 122.8 billion yen, supported by growth in DS and divestitures in\nLS.\nThe equity ratio improved to 35%, up more than five percentage points.\nP10 Statement of Cash Flows (CF)\n\n\n\n\nFree cash flow improved significantly, reflecting both improved profitability and\ncontinued strategic investment.\nOperating cash flow for FY2025 was 61.9 billion yen. Compared with the previous fiscal\nyear, cash flow increased significantly, supported by strong performance in EM and\ngreater stability in LS.\nCash flow from investing activities was positive at 72.2 billion yen. While capital\nexpenditures, primarily in EM, resulted in cash outflows, these were more than offset by\nproceeds from business divestitures.\nFree cash flow was 134.1 billion yen. Even excluding proceeds from business transfers,\nfree cash flow remained positive. The company used the cash generated from free cash\nflow to reduce debt. Cash and cash equivalents at fiscal year-end were 83.0 billion yen.\nP11 Business Highlights: Electronic Materials (1)\n FY2025 delivered both strong revenue growth and record earnings. In advanced devices,\nour MOR has progressed in the adoption for mass production in advanced devices. The\nrevenue also expanded significantly in FY2025, further strengthening the company’s\ncompetitive position.\n Global collaboration accelerated. In addition to close engagement with device\nmanufacturers, our customers, the company further strengthened global partnerships to\nenhance business competitiveness. These included joint development with Lam\nResearch, which had already been announced, collaboration with equipment\nmanufacturers such as Applied Materials, and initiatives with IBM and research\n3\n1-9-2, Higashi-Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo 105-8640 JAPAN\nTel : +81-3-6218-3500 Fax : +81-3-6218-3682\nhttp://www.jsr.co.jp\ninstitutions such as imec.\n The company is making proactive investments, including the construction of a new\nadvanced lithography plant in Taiwan, the establishment of a CMP materials\ndevelopment site, and the launch of a new MOR plant in Korea. These efforts have\nfurther strengthened the service structure for customers in Asia.\nP12 Business Highlights: Electronic Materials (2)\n In FY2025, revenue grew 24% YoY. In lithography, EUV and MOR delivered significant\ngrowth.\n In Process & Deposition Materials, CMP and ALD precursors handled by YAMANAKA\nHUTECH CORPORATION, which was acquired in FY2024, also achieved significant\ngrowth.\n In Advanced Electronic Materials, thick-film resists for advanced packaging and low-\ndielectric resin materials for substrates delivered significant growth.\nP13 Business Highlights: Display/Optical\n In the Display Solutions business, profitability is being enhanced through high-market-\nshare products in LCD and OLED materials. The share of new products is also increasing,\nsupporting future growth.\n In the Optical Solutions business, the company is strengthening its technological\ncapabilities in resin products with superior optical properties, and these efforts are\nbeginning to contribute to earnings.\nP14 Business Highlights: Plastics\n In this business, operated through Techno UMG, we are accelerating the shift toward\nhigher-value-added areas to achieve stable growth.\nP15 Growth Investments\n In EM, the company has strategically strengthened R&D investment for future growth.\nIt has also proactively implemented capital expenditures to expand capacity and\nstrengthen the supply chain, including the establishment of new manufacturing and\ndevelopment sites in Asia, as mentioned earlier.\n Going forward, the company will accelerate growth investments centered on EM. These\ninvestments are intended to achieve the targets of the Mid-Term Business Plan for 2030\nand support sustainable growth beyond that.\n4\n1-9-2, Higashi-Shimbashi, Minato-ku, Tokyo 105-8640 JAPAN\nTel : +81-3-6218-3500 Fax : +81-3-6218-3682\nhttp://www.jsr.co.jp\nP16 Mid-term Business Plan\n FY2025 results were in line with the trajectory set out in the Mid-Term Business Plan.\nThe company will continue to pursue the plan with the goal of achieving core operating\nprofit of 100.0 billion yen by FY2030.\nP17 Outlook\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nIn terms of the business environment, in EM, capital spending by semiconductor\nmanufacturers is expected to increase, supported by robust AI-related investment.\nDevelopment of advanced semiconductors is also progressing.\nIn DIS, steady growth is expected, including in OLED.\nIn PLA, the automotive market is expected to remain broadly flat.\nWith EM continuing to perform strongly, the company expects further growth across the\nbusiness as a whole.\nThrough proactive investment, the company will strengthen global business\ndevelopment and further reinforce its technological leadership.\nThe company will continue to respond fully to increasingly sophisticated customer\nrequirements, including supply stability and quality.\nContinued steady improvement in the financial structure is expected, including the\ntransition away from LBO loans.\nThere is no change to the policy of achieving self-sustaining growth and pursuing a future\nrelisting.\nAs a mid-term business target, the company aims to achieve core operating profit of\n100.0 billion yen by 2030.\nThank you very much for your attention.\n5",
