    "content_text": "Home \r\nInvestors \r\nAnnual Report 2025 \r\nRecommend Facebook LinkedIn \nAnnual report 2025\r\nThe fiscal year 2025 was marked by various challenges for Jenoptik, particularly from the semiconductor equipment and automotive markets. Nevertheless, we have continued to focus on our relevant growth potentials in our core markets of semiconductors, medical technology, metrology and smart mobility, and we look to the future with optimism thanks to our strong growth platforms. \nOverview over the fiscal year 2025\nJenoptik performed well overall in a challenging market environment in 2025.\nDespite a 6 percent decline in revenue , we were able to maintain our profitability at a good level, with an EBITDA margin of 18.4 percent, thanks to cost reduction measures implemented early on.\nWe succeeded in further improving key balance sheet and financial ratios. The Group increased its equity ratio to around 60 percent, and free cash flow before interest and taxes rose by approximately 50 million euros.\nThe Executive Board and Supervisory Board will propose a dividend &nbsp;payout of 0.40 euros per share to the Annual General Meeting.\nThe Group&rsquo;s organizational structure has been realigned more closely with our growth areas of semiconductors, medical technology, metrology, and smart mobility.\nWith the opening of the new fab&nbsp; for innovative micro-optics in Dresden, Germany, an important foundation was laid to realize further growth potential in this area.\nOur approach to sustainability :&nbsp;As an &ldquo;enabler,&rdquo; we use our expertise and innovative products to make an important contribution to overcome social and climate challenges, enable customers worldwide to contribute more efficiently and sustainably to conserving resources and protecting the climate.\nOutlook : We expect to return to a growth path in fiscal year 2026.\nKey figures\nRevenue\r\nmillion euros\r\nEBITDA\r\nmillion euros\r\nOrder intake\r\nmillion euros\r\nDividend per share\r\ncents (AGM approval pending)\r\nMore key figures \nCFO Dr. Prisca Havranek-Kosicek \n&ldquo;For fiscal year 2026, we expect to return to growth. We remain firmly convinced that our photonics product portfolio offers significant profitable growth potential in the markets we address.&rdquo;\nForecast report (download PDF) \nHighlights from the 2025 fiscal year\r\nInauguration of our new fab in Dresden \nAfter around two and a half years of construction, Jenoptik has completed its largest single investment in recent history. \nlearn more \r\nExpansion of the optics manufacturing in Jena \nJenoptik invests in high-end manufacturing facility for semiconductor optics at the production campus in Jena-G&ouml;schwitz. \nlearn more \r\nJordan invests in smart mobility technology \nA contract with the Greater Amman Municipality allows for the roll-out of Jenoptik&rsquo;s advanced traffic safety systems across the capital city. \nlearn more \r\nA stronger focus on future markets \nA new F-theta lens was specially developed for the high-precision creation of complex structures in 3D printing. \nlearn more \r\nSupervisory Board extends Executive Board contracts \nThe Supervisory Board of JENOPTIK AG extende the contracts of Executive Board member Dr. Ralf Kuschnereit and CFO Dr. Prisca Havranek-Kosicek ahead of schedule by five years each. \nlearn more \r\nprevious \r\nnext \r\nRead more news \nExecutive Board member Dr. Ralf Kuschnereit \n&ldquo;We are convinced that our key customers and, as their supplier and partner, Jenoptik as well, will benefit significantly from the megatrends of digitization, health, mobility, and sustainability.&rdquo;\nExecutive Board letter to shareholders (download PDF) \nAnnual Report 2025 (full)\r\n(PDF | 4,28 MB) \r\nInformation for the shareholders\r\n(PDF | 0,59 MB) \r\nGroup management report\r\n(PDF | 2,06 MB) \r\nConsolidated financial statement\r\n(PDF | 1,00 MB) \r\nConsolidated statement of income\r\n(XLSX | 0,02 MB) \r\nConsolidated statement of financial position\r\n(XLSX | 0,02 MB) \r\nConsolidated statement of cash flows\r\n(XLSX | 0,02 MB) \r\nResults presentation\r\n(PDF | 0,64 MB) \r\nPress release from March 25, 2026\r\n(PDF | 0,15 MB) \r\nSustainability report\r\n(PDF | 0,98 MB) \r\nExecutive Board letter to the shareholders\r\n(PDF | 0,14 MB)",
