    "content_text": "09/01/2026 Lifting Without Consequences\nSchmalz is expanding its portfolio of ergonomically designed handling solutions with the forward bend exoskeleton NEXO Pro. It reduces strain on the lower back during bending and lifting movements by up to 30 percent—without the need for an external power source, a rechargeable battery, or maintenance.\nThe forward bend exoskeleton NEXO Pro makes order picking easier and reduces strain caused by frequent bending and lifting of various items.\nBack pain is one of the most common causes of absences from work in physically demanding occupations. The forward bend exoskeleton NEXO Pro addresses this issue: It reduces muscle strain and thus fatigue, accelerates recovery, and maintains performance throughout the entire shift. For companies, this means fewer absences and more stable staffing levels, even during peak periods. Furthermore, the use of exoskeletons strengthens employer branding: physically demanding jobs become more attractive when technical support is visibly available.\nDeveloped from real-world experience\nIn recent years, Schmalz has supported the use of exoskeletons in real-world scenarios, such as in logistics, woodworking, and metalworking. Feedback from these deployments has been directly incorporated into the development of the forward bend exoskeleton NEXO Pro. The result is a product designed to meet the actual requirements of users: quick to put on, self-adjusting, and ready to use right away.\nPassive. Lightweight. Reliable\nThe NEXO Pro forward bend exoskeleton operates purely mechanically. A feeder system absorbs the force when bending forward and returns it when straightening up. It supports the back during trunk flexion without putting additional compression on the spine, thereby reducing strain on the muscles. Thanks to breathable, washable materials, it is suitable for use both inside and outside. The on/off function can be operated with a single hand movement. An audible cue confirms the switching state even without looking at the device. Users can adjust all girders and operator handles themselves without tools, as well as set the intensity and the point at which support begins. The exoskeleton is available in two sizes.\nRelief That Pays Off\nThe forward bend exoskeleton NEXO Pro is suitable for all tasks that require repetitive bending and lifting movements. Typical applications include order picking and warehouse logistics, loading and unloading machines in wood and metalworking, as well as mounting and finishing tasks on large-scale components. The system also provides reliable support in goods receiving and output, including confined spaces such as truck cargo areas and containers.\nThe NEXO Control Unit is used to activate, adjust, and control the start of assistance and the level of assistance.\nEmployees are assisted by the forward bend exoskeleton NEXO Pro when loading and unloading metalworking machines, which reduces the strain on their backs.\nThe forward bend exoskeleton NEXO Pro reduces strain on the back and shoulders when handling heavy wooden parts and promotes healthy working habits in everyday work.\nMedia contact\nThe Schmalz press team will be happy to answer any questions you may have.\npresse@schmalz.de \nForward Bend Exoskeleton NEXO Pro\nLess Back Strain, More Power: How Exoskeletons Create a Connection Between Health and Productivity\nShow more Show less \nNEW\nForward Bend Exoskeletons NEXO Pro\nPassive exoskeleton with a stable structure\nSupports the lower back muscles\nUp to 30% less strain on the back\nApprox. 5 kg weight\nShow category",
