    "content_text": "Hydro brings high-recycled aluminium to General Motors EV with Hydro CIRCAL\nGeneral Motors’ Cadillac OPTIQ will feature a front bumper system made with Hydro CIRCAL, an advanced aluminium alloy composed of at least 75 percent post‑consumer scrap produced at Hydro’s newest U.S. recycling facility in Cassopolis, Michigan.\nThe 2026 Cadillac OPTIQ with Hydro CIRCAL recycled aluminium. (Photo: General Motors) \nHydro, automotive supplier Shape Corp. and General Motors are demonstrating how aluminium from end-of-life products can be recycled and returned to new automotive applications, supporting increased circularity in the mobility sector.\nThe collaboration marks one of the first U.S. implementations of Hydro CIRCAL in a structural, safety‑critical automotive application.\n“By bringing recycled aluminium back into demanding vehicle applications, we can reduce embedded emissions, strengthen material circularity and make better use of the resources already in circulation,” says Duncan Pitchford, Vice President Recycling, Hydro Aluminum Metal.\nHigh-recycled aluminium for automotive applications\nHydro will supply Hydro CIRCAL from its U.S. recycling facility in Cassopolis, Michigan. Shape Corp. will engineer and assemble the front bumper system to GM specifications, with integration into the Cadillac OPTIQ platform.\nBy sourcing recycled aluminium locally and making it in Michigan, GM strengthens U.S. production and supply chain resilience while demonstrating how regional recycling networks can return valuable materials to new vehicle applications.\nHydro CIRCAL uses aluminium recovered from end-of-life products such as vehicles, windows, doors and electrical cables. The material is remelted and transformed into new aluminium products through Hydro's recycling operations.\nIllustration showing the front bumper beam, a crash-management component, positioned at the front of the vehicle. General Motors has selected Hydro CIRCAL for this application in the Cadillac OPTIQ. \nThe product offers a market-leading carbon footprint of 1.5 kg CO₂e per kg of aluminium, or lower, while meeting demanding automotive requirements for strength, energy absorption, corrosion resistance and formability. The low carbon footprint means Hydro CIRCAL delivers an estimated 70 percent reduction in CO₂ emissions compared to the North American average for primary aluminium production.\nHow the component is used\nThe front bumper beam is a structural crash‑management part located at the front of the vehicle, behind the visible bumper cover. It absorbs and distributes impact energy in collisions to help protect passengers, pedestrians and critical EV systems, an application where material choice is essential.\nUsing Hydro CIRCAL in this part demonstrates that aluminum with high post‑consumer recycled content can meet demanding performance needs while helping lower embedded carbon footprint.\nAbout Hydro CIRCAL\nHydro CIRCAL is Hydro’s recycled aluminium product line containing a minimum 75 percent post‑consumer scrap with third‑party (DNV) verification. Each batch carries verified documentation to support customer traceability and reporting. In North America, Hydro produces Hydro CIRCAL at its U.S. recycling operations, including Cassopolis, Michigan.\nPublished: August 5, 2026\nLearn more\nHydro CIRCAL recycled aluminium\nAluminium in automotive\nHydro's roadmap to net-zero\nContact\nMarius Motrøen \nCommunication Manager, Hydro Aluminium Metal\nmarius.motroen@hydro.com \n+47 916 97 764 \nSubscribe to news and press releases from Hydro",
