    "content_text": "Newsroom\nWomen in industry\nArkema tackles the risk of the &ldquo;glass ceiling,&rdquo; supports the advancement of its female employees, encourages the emergence of female talent in the industry, and has set targets for increasing the proportion of women in senior management and executive positions.\nFind our latest news on this topic here.\n&nbsp;\nSubscribe to our news \nOur latest news \nSep \n03 \n2024 \nAppointment \nWomen in industry \nBelgin K&ouml;se appointed Senior Vice-President of the Construction & Consumer business line within Arkema's Adhesive Solutions segment\nBelgin Köse has joined Arkema as Senior Vice-President of the Construction & Consumer ...\nRead more \nSenior Vice-President of the Construction & Consumer business line within Arkema's Adhesive Solutions segment\"> \narkema-belgin-kose.jpg \nAug \n29 \n2024 \nFinance \nAppointment \nWomen in industry \nAppointments to Arkema&rsquo;s executive committee \nSophie Fouillat has been appointed as the Group’s Executive Vice-President, Strategy ...\nRead more \nArkema&rsquo;s executive committee \"> \narkema-la-defense-hq.jpg \nFeb \n24 \n2023 \nAppointment \nWomen in industry \nVirginie Gu&eacute;rin appointed Arkema Vice President Institutional Affairs \nSince 1 st February Virginie Guérin joined Arkema to be appointed on ...\nRead more \nArkema Vice President Institutional Affairs \"> \narkema-virginie-guerin.jpg \nJun \n29 \n2022 \nCSR \nFinance \nAppointment \nWomen in industry \nEmmanuelle Bromet appointed Arkema Sustainable Development Vice President \nA graduate of Chimie ParisTech and École Nationale Supérieure du ... \nRead more \nappointed Arkema Sustainable Development Vice President \"> \nemmanuelle-bromet-arkema-2.jpg \nSee more news \nEncouraging talented women\nOur actions \nAn internal network for promoting women\nWomen@Arkema \nPress contacts \nFor any additional information and/or visuals requests, the press relations team will reply quickly.\nContact us \nNewsroom\nBack to the home page",
