    "content_text": "Newsroom Bayer\nSeptember\n17 , \n2026\n| \r\n15:00 PM \r\nEurope/Amsterdam \r\nRobigo and Leaps by Bayer Announce Series A Financing to Advance Engineered Biologicals That Protect Yields and Reduce Costs \r\nRobigo&rsquo;s engineered microbes for combatting Sudden Death Syndrome in soybeans match the performance of commercially available chemistries at half the cost, targeting launch in 2028 / The second product in development, targeting the #1 fungal &hellip; \nRead more\r\nTags\nExport-LatestNews \r\nResearch & Innovation \r\nCrop Protection \r\nCompany \r\nBusiness & Finance \r\nSeptember\n17 , \n2026\n| \r\n08:30 AM \r\nEurope/Amsterdam \r\nU.S. FDA approves finerenone for new indication in patients with chronic kidney disease associated with type 1 diabetes \r\nNot intended for U.S. and UK Media\nKerendia&trade; is the first FDA-approved treatment option in more than 30 years for adults with chronic kidney disease (CKD) associated with type 1 diabetes (T1D) / Approval addresses an important unmet need for a population at increased risk of &hellip; \nRead more\r\nTags\nDocCheck-EN \r\nExport-LatestNews \r\nPharmaceuticals \r\nExport-PH \r\nExport-TopNews \r\nSeptember\n09 , \n2026\n| \r\n20:20 PM \r\nEurope/Amsterdam \r\nU.S. FDA grants accelerated approval to Bayer’s targeted therapy sevabertinib as a first-line treatment option for adults with HER2-mutant non-small cell lung cancer \r\nNot intended for U.S. and UK Media\nAccelerated approval of sevabertinib for patients with advanced HER2-mutant non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) follows FDA Priority Review and Breakthrough Therapy Designations, and reflects the potential for sevabertinib to provide substantial &hellip; \nRead more\r\nTags\nDocCheck-EN \r\nSPECIALIZED PRESS \r\nExport-Asia & Pacific \r\nExport-LatestNews \r\nExport-PH \r\nSeptember\n09 , \n2026\n| \r\n14:00 PM \r\nEurope/Amsterdam \r\nBayer and Neste close commercial agreement to jointly scale newgold® winter canola for biofuels production \r\nCommitment aims to support the growth of winter canola in the Southern Great Plains of the U.S., as a feedstock for renewable diesel and sustainable aviation fuel \nRead more\r\nTags\nExport-CS \r\nExport-IR \r\nExport-LatestNews \r\nInvestor News \r\nCrop Science \r\nSeptember\n09 , \n2026\n| \r\n08:30 AM \r\nEurope/Amsterdam \r\nBayer initiates Phase II study of investigational GIRK4 inhibitor in patients with atrial fibrillation \r\nNot intended for U.S. and UK Media\nGIRK4 (BAY 3670549) is an investigational highly selective G-protein-coupled inwardly rectifying potassium channel 4 (GIRK4) inhibitor being evaluated as a potential new approach to control the electrical activity of cardiomyocytes in patients &hellip; \nRead more\r\nTags\nDocCheck-EN \r\nSPECIALIZED PRESS \r\nExport-LatestNews \r\nExport-PH \r\nPharmaceuticals \r\nSeptember\n02 , \n2026\n| \r\n14:00 PM \r\nEurope/Amsterdam \r\nBayer advances combined seed and crop protection pipeline and enters phase of blockbuster launches \r\nCommercialization of two blockbusters already started, with additional launches expected over the next years / Bayer announces genome-edited standable soy and development of herbicide tolerant trait to correspond with Icafolin, a unique crop &hellip; \nRead more\r\nTags\nExport-CS \r\nExport-IR \r\nExport-LatestNews \r\nExport-TopNews \r\nCrop Science \r\nAugust\n30 , \n2026\n| \r\n13:50 PM \r\nEurope/Amsterdam \r\nPhase III REVEAL Study with Investigational PET Radiotracer Iodine 124 Evuzamitide Presented as Late-Breaker at ESC 2026 \r\nNot intended for U.S. and UK Media – European Society of Cardiology (ESC) Congress 2026:\nPivotal study met primary endpoints in the assessment of sensitivity and specificity for the diagnosis of cardiac amyloidosis based on visual scan interpretation / Phase III results in patients with suspected cardiac amyloidosis were presented at &hellip; \nRead more\r\nTags\nDocCheck-EN \r\nSPECIALIZED PRESS \r\nExport-LatestNews