    "link_rank": 0,
    "content_text": "Information for shareholders of JENOPTIK AG\non data protection with regard to registered\nshares\nThe following information instructs you about the processing of your personal data by\nJENOPTIK AG, Jena (hereinafter referred to as “we”, “us” or “the company”) and the rights to\nwhich you are entitled in accordance with data protection law.\nYour personal data is all the information that may be assigned to you as an identified or\nidentifiable natural person (hereinafter referred to as “personal data”), such as your name or\ncontact data. We take the protection of your personal data very seriously and process your\ndata in accordance with the General Data Processing Regulation EU 2016/679 (“GDPR”)\nand the applicable national data protection laws.\nWho is responsible for the data processing?\nThe person responsible (“Controller”) within the meaning of the GDPR and other national\ndata protection laws of the Member States of the EU as well as other data protection\nregulations is:\nJENOPTIK AG\nCarl-Zeiss-Str. 1\nDE-07743 Jena, Germany\nTelephone: +49 3641 65-0\nTelefax: +49 3641 424514\nEmail: ir@jenoptik.com\nWebsite: www.jenoptik.com\nrepresented by the Executive Board:\nDr Stefan Traeger (Chairman) and Hans-Dieter Schumacher,\nregistered in the commercial register at the district court of Jena, HRB 200146.\nThe Data Protection Officer of the controller is:\nMrs. Nicole Meerstedt\nData Protection Officer of JENOPTIK AG\nCarl-Zeiß-Straße 1\n07743 Jena, Germany\nE-mail: data-protection.joag@jenoptik.com\nWhat personal data do we process? For what purposes and\non what legal basis do we process your personal data?\nFrom whom do we receive your data?\nThe shares of JENOPTIK AG are registered shares. In the case of registered shares, section\n67 of the German Stock Corporation Act stipulates that these must be recorded in the\ncompany's share register, stating the name, date of birth, address and number of shares held\nby the shareholder. The shareholder shall generally be required to provide the company with\nthis information. Referred to a provision in the bylaws of JENOPTIK AG shareholders shall\nalso provide their email address, to enable a direct dialogue between the company and the\nshareholders.\nThe banks involved in the acquisition or custody of your JENOPTIK AG registered shares\nregularly pass on to us the information relevant for managing the share register. This is done\nvia Clearstream Banking Aktiengesellschaft, Mergenthalerallee 61, DE-65760 Eschborn,\nwhich as the central securities depository is responsible for the technical settlement of\nsecurities trades and the storage of shares for the banks. Should you sell your shares, the\nbank of the new purchaser will inform us of this.\nThe following personal data will be transmitted to us by the banks:\n‐\n‐\n‐\n‐\n‐\n‐\n‐\nFirst name, last name of the shareholder\nDate of birth\nAddress of the shareholder\nNumber of shares\nAmount of shares owned by the shareholder\nEmail address of the shareholder\nInformation of whether the shares are held by the shareholder itself or by a third party\nWe process your personal data exclusively for the purpose of managing the statutory share\nregister of JENOPTIK AG.\nThe legal basis for the processing of your personal data is Art. 6.1.c of the GDPR in\nconnection with our obligations under the German Stock Corporation Act.\nShould we wish to process your personal data for a purpose other than that mentioned\nabove, we shall inform you of this in advance within the framework of the statutory provisions\nand only arrange for this to be carried out if we are permitted to do so by a statutory\nauthorization pursuant to Art. 6 of the GDPR.\nTo which categories of recipients do we pass on your\ninformation?\nExternal service providers:\nWe use partly external service providers for the administration and technical management of\nthe share register (share register service company, IT service provider) as well as for the\nhandling of shareholders’ meetings (AGM service provider). External service providers who\nwork on our behalf are contractually bound as data processors in accordance with Article\n28.3 of the GDPR. Computershare Deutschland GmbH & Co. KG, Elsenheimerstraße 61,\nDE-80687 Munich, is authorized to manage the share register of JENOPTIK AG, and\nperforms this duty as a data processor within the meaning of Art. 28 of the GDPR.\nPage 2/3\nOther recipients:\nIn addition, we may transfer your personal data to other recipients in accordance with Art.\n6.1.c of the GDPR, insofar as we are legally required to do so, such as to official bodies to\nfulfill statutory reporting obligations (e.g. when exceeding statutory voting right thresholds), or\nprovided that another legal basis as per Art. 6 of the GDPR entitles us to transfer your\npersonal data.\nFor how long do we store your personal data?\nWe delete your personal data as soon as it is no longer required for the above-mentioned\npurposes and there is no statutory retention obligation regarding this data. Statutes such as\nthe German Commercial Code, the Fiscal Code of Germany and the German Money\nLaundering Act specify corresponding burdens of proof and periods of retention. The\nretention periods are regularly up to ten years.\nHow do we transfer data to non-European countries?\nWe do not intend to transfer your personal data to a third country outside the European\nEconomic Area (EEA) or to an international organization. Should we pass on personal data\nto service providers outside the European Economic Area (EEA), the transfer shall only take\nplace if the third country has been confirmed to have an appropriate level of data protection\nby the EU Commission or if other appropriate data protection guarantees (e.g. binding\ninternal company data protection regulations or agreements on the standard contractual\nclauses of the EU Commission) are in place. You may request detailed information on this\nand the level of data protection from our service providers in third countries at the above\nspecified contact information.\nWhat rights do you have as a data subject?\nAccording to Art. 15 of the GDPR, you may request that the Controller named in this data\nprivacy statement provides you with any information stored about you. In addition, under\ncertain conditions you may request the rectification (Art. 16 of GDPR) or erasure (Art. 17 of\nGDPR) of your personal data. You may also have a right to restrict the processing of your\npersonal data in accordance with Art. 18 of the GDPR and a right to have your personal data\nreleased to you in a structured, commonly used and machine-readable format in accordance\nwith Art. 20 GDPR. Ultimately, you also have a right of objection in accordance with the\nconditions regulated in Art. 21 of the GDPR.\nWould you like to complain about the handling of your data?\nYou may contact JENOPTIK AG's Data Protection Officer mentioned above or a data\nprotection supervisory authority. The supervisory authority responsible for us is:\nThe State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information Thuringia\nPO box 900455\nDE-99107 Erfurt, Germany\n* * * * *\nPage 3/3",
