    "content_text": "Robust results,\nGuidance upgraded\nMerck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany\nQ2 2026 results\nKai Beckmann, CEO\nHelene von Roeder, CFO\nAugust 6, 2026\nAgenda\nExecutive Summary\nFinancial Overview\nOutlook & Guidance\n2 Merck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany, Q2 2026 Results Presentation | August 6, 2026\n01\nExecutive\nsummary\nStrategy Recap – Execution Underway\nAnnouncement of Strong momentum in New Metrology &\nplanned acquisition Rare Diseases Inspection manufacturing\nof Bio-Techne portfolio site near Grenoble\nFocus on Shift selected Leverage Scale and source\nhigh-growth product portfolio toward platformed innovation via\nvalue drivers integrated workflow capabilities M&A and in-licensing\nsolutions across businesses\n4 Merck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany, Q2 2026 Results Presentation | August 6, 2026 The colored cubes indicate activities that map to one or more streams.\nHighlights: Process Solutions and Semi Solutions Fuel Organic Growth\nOperations\nQ2 YoY organic sales growth\nLife Science:\n Temporary uplift in PS growth (+15%) continued\n Solid growth in AS; slight growth contribution from DS\n Strong LS sales (+8%) supported by all regions\nHealthcare:\n Rare Diseases growth in line with guidance (PF +5pp)\n Cardiometabolic and F&E around stable\n HC sales decline (-3%) driven by Specialty Care\nElectronics:\n Double-digit growth of Semi Solutions (+17%)\n Optronics around stable amid increasing headwinds\n EL growth accelerated (+12%)\nGroup Financials\nQ2 organic sales: +4.1%\nQ2 organic EBITDA pre: +9.3%\n2026 Guidance:\nNet sales: €21.0 bn to €21.8 bn\nEBITDA pre: €5.9 bn to €6.3 bn\nEPS pre: €7.90 to €8.60\nNet financial debt to EBITDA pre:\n1.5x on Jun 30, 2026\nAcronym(s): PS = Process Solutions; AS= Advanced Solutions; LS= Life Science;\nPF= Portfolio Effect; F&E = Fertility & Endocrinology; HC = Healthcare;EL=\n5 Merck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany, Q2 2026 Results Presentation | August 6, 2026 Electronics; EPS= Earnings Per Share.\nDel