d\nprocesses\nHealth\nEnvironmental footprint\nreduction\n17 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\n\n\n\n\n\nCultivate an open\ndialogue and close\nrelations with our\nstakeholders\nEthics\nHuman rights\nDiversity & Employee\ndevelopment\nResponsible value chain\nCorporate citizenship\nINNOVATION THROUGH 6 FOCUSED R&D PLATFORMS DEDICATED TO SUSTAINABILITY\nNew energies Lightweight materials Bio-based products Electronics solutions Water management Home efficiency and\nand design insulation\nPORTFOLIO SUSTAINABILITY ASSESSMENT RESEARCH & INNOVATION CIRCULAR ECONOMY\n44% of products portfolio assessed at end In 2019, 149 patent applications 9% of sales from products\n2019, 46% of which is significantly linked to sustainable development, made from renewable raw material\ncontributing to UN Sustainable representing 67% of the total number of\nDevelopment Goals patent applications. Virtucycle™ recycling program enables\ncustomers to partner with Arkema in\nObjective to achieve 100% portfolio open-loop and closed-loop initiatives for\nsustainability assessment 10,268 patents in force specialty polymers recycling projects\n18 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nSTRONG COMMITMENT ON CLIMATE AND ENVIRONMENT\nCLIMATE CLIMATE PLAN ENVIRONMENT\nCommitment to Paris agreement New targets for 2030\nand Science-Based Target\ntrajectory well below 2°C AIR WATER ENERGY\nGHG EMISSIONS in kteq. CO 2\nGreenhouse gas emissions\n6,480 (GHG) new target for 2030 -65% -60% -20%\nvs 2012 vs 2012 vs 2012\n4,720\n4,087 in volatile organic in chemical oxygen in net energy\n≤ 2,950 compounds (VOC) demand (COD) purchases intensity\nemissions intensity intensity\nkt eq. CO 2\nPerformance 2019 (vs 2012)\n(-38% vs 2015)\n-40% -50% -9%\n2012 est. 2015 2019\n19 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nCULTIVATE AN OPEN DIALOGUE WITH OUR STAKEHOLDERS\nSUSTAINABLE SUPPLY COMMUNITY RELATIONS\n>1600 1000\nsuppliers ~ initiatives\nassessed accounting for per year with neighboring\nmore than 50%