ment of such project.\n• Post completion of the “Eligible Project”, Arkema intends to provide a\n• Arkema intends to allocate the proceeds to the “Eligible Project” with no\nmeasure of the impact of the “Eligible Project” on climate change in tons\nmore than a 2-year look-back period and fully within 36 months of the\nof CO 2 avoided, through an LCA analysis validated by a third party.\nissuance of the Green Bonds.\n*InternationalCapital Market Association Green Bond Principles 2018\n**Detailed eligibility criteria for each Project category can be found in Arkema’sGreen Bond Framework under section 2.1\n23 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nRILSAN® POLYAMIDE 11 – AN ELIGIBLE GREEN INVESTMENT\nWholly derived from renewable feedstock – castor beans\nCarbon footprint of Rilsan® PA 11 significantly lower when\ncompared to comparable polymers with fossil fuel feedstock*\nA sustainable high performance polymer - used in demanding\ndurable applications and not for single consumer use\nFully recyclable\nSingapore plant will be built in line with best international\nstandards of safety and environmental performance\n*Carbon footprint – calculated in accordance with ISO 14067:2018, 14040 and 14044 and to be validated by third party\n24 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nARKEMA’S SINGAPORE PROJECT\nProject Scope\nCASTOR PLANT CASTOR SEEDS CASTOR OIL AMINO 11 RILSAN® POLYAMIDE 11\nNo Food Competition\nProfitable for Farmers\nDriving Sustainable Farming\nNo Deforestation\nGrows inMarginal Soil\nA major A 11 production and PA 11 polymerization investment – moving closer to\nthe castor supply and to Asian customers.\n\n\n\n\nArkema only producer in the world of 100% biobased amino 11 & polyamide 11\nWorld scale plant in Singapore dedicated to producing amino 11\n(~50% increase of worldwide capacities)\nProject also includes production of Rilsan® PA 11 on the same site\nScheduled to come on stream in 2022\n25 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nRILSAN® POLYAMIDE 11, NOT JUST BIOBASED\nThe highest performing\npolyamide range\nBiobased, renewable\nLow carbon footprint\nNo competition with food\nNo deforestation\nA proven\nlegacy of 70 Profitable crop\nyears Sustainable farming\nRecyclable\n26 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nArkema and its partners in the\nPragati initiative are driving\nsustainable farming in India,\nwhere 80% of the world’s castor\nbeans originate\nSUSTAINABLE SOURCING: CASTOR CROP\nTOP 4\nuses for Castor oil\n700,000\n800,000\nTOP 2\nperceived sustainability\nadvantages of castor beans\n47%\n5\n27 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nNumbers of castor beans farmers in India\nNumbers of hectares of land dedicated to\ncastor farming in India\nNaturally drought resistant\nDoes not compete with food chain for\nhumans or animals\nOf the weight of castor bean is captured as\ncastor oil. The remainder is generally\nrepurposed as a fertilizer\nFarmers typically harvest castor pods at\nleast 5 times per year 120 to 210 days after\nplanting\nDRIVEN BY OUR MARKETS\nHigh Performance\nSports Shoes 3D Printing\nLightweight Efficient Processing\nEnergy Return Superior Impact\nDurable Flexibility Proven Legacy\nAutomotive\nLightweight\nMetal Replacement\nNew Energy\nVehicles\nLIGHTWEIGHT RECYCLABLE\nConsumer Consumer\nProducts Electronics\nDurable Laptop and\nEyewear Mobile Phone\nDesign Flexibility Components\nEco Design\nRENEWABLE HIGHLY DURABLE\n28 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nBIOBASED PA11 VS. FOSSIL POLYMERS: FAVORABLE CLIMATE CHANGE IMPACT\nRilsan® PA11 with 30% Rilsan® PA11 Panel of petrobased\nrecycled content polymers\nLower dependence on fossil based raw materials\nClimate change (kg eq. CO 2 /kg)\nStandard ISO 14040-14044-14067\n29 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW\nA VIRTUOUS CYCLE FOR “END OF LIFE”\nRECYCLING PROCESS\nNew recycling\ninitiative with partners\nand key customers\n30 ARKEMA OCTOBER 2020 GREEN BOND ROADSHOW",
