    "content_text": "Schmalz Acres celebrates America 250 with corn maze and expanded activities\nby Emily Matesic, FOX 11 News\nMon, August 31, 2026 at 5:33 PM Updated Mon, August 31, 2026 at 8:29 PM \n17 VIEW ALL PHOTOS \nSchmalz Acres Adventure Zone and Sprangers Orchard, in Kaukauna, have expanded the family-friendly activities they offer during the Fall. August 31, 2026. (Emily Matesic/WLUK)\n0 Comment \nShare \ntopics: \nSchmalz Acres \nAmerica 250 \nCorn maze \nKaukauna \nAdventure zone \nApple picking \nServicemembers \nPolice officers \nKAUKAUNA (WLUK) - It may feel like summer, but fall is in the air. \nKids are in school, football season in underway, and it's time to pick apples and find your way through a corn maze.\nThe finishing touches are being put on the expanded adventure zone at Schmalz Acres and Sprangers Orchard in Kaukauna.\nWLUK\n\"It is so exciting to be part of this expansion, to bring in more families, to have more employees be part of this on a regular basis,\" said Andy Christenson with Schmalz Acres.\nThe more than 60 acres of property is about more than just apples. An entire array of family-friendly activities are set to open the first weekend in September.\nAccording to Christenson, \"We've added more for interaction with the kids for families to have a full day here at the orchard.\"\nThere's of course apple picking and pumpkins and sunflowers, but the adventure zone also includes basketball, duck races, a giant sand pile and plenty of hay.\nBut the biggest, in size, attraction is the Schmalz corn maze. Acre after acre of corn planted and then cut into a design.\nSchmalz working with a company out of Pennsylvania on theme to help celebrate America 250.\n\"We got America across the top and then the letters of 250,\" said Christenson. He continued, \"The corn bridge is right in the middle of that 250 and the rest makes up soldiers that are holding a flag. So quite significant from purposeful standpoint of America turning 250.\"\nIt's not just the corn maze celebrating America 250, Schmalz is also honoring America by offering free admission to police officers, servicemembers and veterans.\nAnd everyone who takes on the maze should be ready to play its game.\n\"There are game stations throughout 22 of them where you will have to find those game stations in order to create your or complete I should say, your game map and at the end of that you might get a sticker,\" added Christenson.\nWhile the prizes are nice, Schmalz is hoping visitors to the adventure zone leave with memories to last a lifetime.\nSchmalz Acres Adventure Zone will be open every weekend in September and October.\nTrending\nOshkosh man arrested after police say he threatened victim, 3 children with gun\nOSHKOSH (WLUK) -- A 45-year-old Oshkosh man was arrested after police say he threatened a person and three children with a gun Friday night.\nArrest made in 1995 cold case murder\nThe former roommate of a man last seen in 1995 has been charged with murder.\nLambeau Field's concessions 3rd best in NFL, analysis finds\nFans going to Thursday night's Green Bay Packers home opener will have a chance to try some of the NFL's best concessions, at least according to one analysis.\nTwo Rivers celebrates 35th Annual Ethnic Fest, only 2nd forced inside due to rain\nThe 35th Annual Two Rivers Ethnic Fest had to be moved indoors Saturday. Two Rivers Main Street says Saturday was the second time it was affected by the rain.\nDry and blustery Sunday as rain moves away\nAfter a soggy Saturday and Saturday evening for many, we're finally drying out as we close the weekend.Look for a mix of clouds and sun today with a high around\nNEWS IN PHOTOS:\n\" Local \" \n8 \nNEW Nearly 2 months after Fox Valley tornado, free pet supply hub fills ongoing need \n4 \n35th Community First Fox Cities Marathon announces winners \n9 \nTwo Rivers celebrates 35th Annual Ethnic Fest, only 2nd forced inside due to rain \n6 \nKids can become part of the art inside the Building for Kids new exhibit",
