    "content_text": "ABL Diagnostics discloses 16.1 million shares and voting rights structure \n1 min read | Published on 27 Aug 2026, 09:58 PM | Updated on 27 Aug 2026, 09:58 PM \nReviewed by Anirudha B ScanX News Team \nAdd as a preferred source on Google \nKey Highlights \nTotal share capital comprises 16,114,656 shares as of August 12, 2026\nTheoretical voting rights stand at 30,501,420 due to double voting provisions\nExercisable voting rights total 30,471,564 for active shareholder decisions\nDouble voting rights apply to shares held by same shareholder for two years\npowered by \n*this image is generated using AI for illustrative purposes only.\nABL Diagnostics (Euronext: ABLD) disclosed its share capital and voting rights structure as of August 12, 2026, in a regulatory filing. The Paris-listed molecular biology diagnostics firm reported a total share capital comprising 16,114,656 shares.\nThe company’s filing, mandated by Articles L. 233-8 II of the French Commercial Code and Article 223-16 of the AMF General Regulation, provides a breakdown of voting power attached to these shares.\nShare Capital and Voting Rights\nAs per the disclosure, the total number of shares constituting the share capital stands at 16,114,656 . The associated voting rights are detailed below:\nMetric \nCount \nTotal Shares \n16,114,656 \nTheoretical Voting Rights \n30,501,420 \nExercisable Voting Rights \n30,471,564 \nTheoretical voting rights include all shares to which voting rights are attached, even if suspended or deprived. Exercisable voting rights represent those currently active for shareholder decisions.\nDouble Voting Rights Mechanism\nThe disparity between the number of shares and theoretical voting rights stems from a double voting right mechanism. Resolutions adopted on March 23, 2022, grant double voting rights to all fully paid-up shares registered in the name of the same shareholder for at least two years. This provision has been effective since March 23, 2022.\nBusiness Overview\nHeadquartered in Woippy, France, ABL Diagnostics specializes in innovative molecular biology tests. Its core product portfolio includes:\nMolecular polymerase chain reaction (PCR) detection via UltraGene.\nGenotyping by DNA sequencing through DeepChek.\nThe company markets its solutions globally through an internal sales team and exclusive distributors. Key customers include academic clinical pathology laboratories, private reference labs, and researchers.\nRecent strategic moves include the acquisition of TEXCELL’s operations, expanding ABL Diagnostics’ activities in virology, biosafety testing, and biopharmaceutical development support. Additionally, since the second half of 2025, the firm has marketed products from its sister company CDL Pharma under an intra-group strategy agreement.\nDisclaimer: This article is AI-generated using data from ViewTrade. ScanX is not liable for any inaccuracies. \nHow might the double voting rights structure impact potential takeover defenses or future M&A activity for ABL Diagnostics?\nfuzz it \nWhat is the projected revenue contribution from the newly acquired TEXCELL operations in virology and biosafety testing for the upcoming fiscal year?\nfuzz it \nCould the intra-group strategy with CDL Pharma lead to further consolidation within the ABL group or cross-selling opportunities in new therapeutic areas?\nfuzz it \n19 \nRead Next Article",
