    "content_text": "Skyworks Solutions Falls as Chip Selloff Adds Pressure to Qorvo Deal Financing Overhang\nBy: Quiver PriceTracker\nPosted: 3 weeks, 5 days ago / Aug. 25, 2026 4:18 p.m. UTC \nSWKS\nSkyworks Solutions (SWKS) is down 4.0% today. Here is some analysis on what might have caused this price movement.\nAnalysis: The drop appears tied to a mix of company-specific financing overhang and a broader semiconductor selloff. Investors may be reacting to Skyworks’ recent debt issuance and higher expected interest expense tied to its pending Qorvo combination, while chip stocks broadly weakened ahead of Nvidia earnings.\nDetails: Skyworks said in its late-July quarterly release that its September-quarter outlook includes incremental net interest expense related to financing for the pending Qorvo acquisition.\nThe same update introduced a new capital allocation framework, including a $2 billion repurchase authorization and a decision to stop declaring quarterly dividends, which may have been read as a sign that merger financing is reshaping shareholder returns.\nAn August 10 current report showed Skyworks completed a sizable senior notes financing, including 2028, 2032, and 2036 maturities, reinforcing the market’s focus on leverage and deal execution risk.\nThis could also be because semiconductor names were under broad pressure today as investors turned cautious ahead of Nvidia’s results, pulling down multiple chip stocks even without fresh company-specific negatives.\nSources: \nSkyworks Solutions, SEC, The Star\nDisclaimer: This price movement analysis was generated with the help of AI. Please double-check the information provided for mistakes.\nQuiver Alerts\nReceive SWKS Data Alerts\nGet market-moving data, filings, and signals for SWKS in real time.\nSign Up\n$SWKS Hedge Fund Activity\nWe have seen 343 institutional investors add shares of $SWKS stock to their portfolio, and 419 decrease their positions in their most recent quarter.\nHere are some of the la