    "content_text": "BASF Opens Global Superabsorbents Performance Lab in Mumbai\nThe new Mumbai, India, facility will offer technical testing and application support to diaper and hygiene product customers worldwide.\nBASF’s Global Performance Lab for diapers and superabsorbents (SAP) opened in Mumbai, India, in August 2026. It provides technical and application services to superabsorbent customers globally. The lab can perform more than 30 testing methods in a 200 square-meter lab area. Designed for SAP as well as for diaper performance and benchmark testing, it supports the co-creation of innovative superabsorbent solutions for baby diapers, adult incontinence products and feminine hygiene applications.\n© BASF\nBASF has inaugurated its new Performance Lab for diapers and superabsorbents (SAP) in Mumbai, which will provide technical and application services to superabsorbent customers globally. The new lab of BASF&rsquo;s Hygiene Solutions business has been established in less than a year and is part of BASF&rsquo;s Innovation Campus Asia Pacific in Mumbai, BASF&rsquo;s second-largest R&D site in Asia Pacific, established in 2017 under BASF Chemicals India.\nBuilding on a global production network for superabsorbents, the Global Technical Service Lab in Mumbai will provide technical support, application expertise, and rapid customer-focused collaboration in one of the world&rsquo;s most dynamic growth markets. The lab will be able to perform more than 30 testing methods in a new 200 square-meter lab area. Designed for SAP as well as for diaper performance and benchmark testing, it will support the co-creation of innovative superabsorbent solutions for baby diapers, adult incontinence products and feminine hygiene applications.\n&ldquo;The opening of the Mumbai Global SAP Performance Lab reflects our commitment to advancing performance, sustainability, and value for our customers all over the world,&rdquo; said Oliver Cullmann, Vice President, Global Marketing & Strategy C3 Value Chain. &ldquo;By creating opportunities for closer collaboration and faster knowledge exchange, we can accelerate innovation and develop solutions that better address the needs of consumers and the market.&rdquo;\nThe Mumbai SAP and Diaper Performance Labs represent more than a new technical facility. It embodies BASF&rsquo;s dedication to customer intimacy, collaboration, speed, and innovation. It will collaborate with the existing Global Product Development Lab for superabsorbents in Ludwigshafen, Germany.\nBASF \ninvestment \nnew facility \nsuperabsorbent polymers \nCompany\nBASF SE \nCarl-Bosch-Straße 38\n67056 Ludwigshafen\nGermany",
