    "content_text": "PCDC celebrates 25 years of economic development in Pflugerville\nExplore Pflugerville - Hutto on the Impact Map stories, offers and more \nJillian Nachtigal \nMore Development news from Pflugerville - Hutto\nDevelopment San Marcos - Buda - Kyle \nKia dealership, Walmart: Check out 5 major Austin-area permits filed this week\n5d ago \nDevelopment Pflugerville - Hutto \n$280M data center coming to Hutto\nMore from Pflugerville - Hutto\nGovernment Georgetown \nWilCo OKs $1.1M archival, preservation plan\n1d ago \nGovernment Pflugerville - Hutto \nHutto City Council votes to end use of Flock Safety license plate readers\nMore from Austin\nBusiness Georgetown \nTexas Roadhouse to open next month in Georgetown\n12h ago \nBusiness Georgetown \nGibson & Co. Salon permanently closed in Georgetown\n1 min read \nPublished August 20, 2026 at 3:25 p.m. CT \nThe Pflugerville Community Development Corporation is celebrating its 25th anniversary on Aug. 20. (Courtesy Pflugerville Community Development Corporation) \nThe Pflugerville Community Development Corporation marked its 25th anniversary of serving the local community by driving economic growth, job creation and infrastructure development to the city on Aug. 20.\nThe big picture \nThe PCDC is a Texas 4B Economic Development Corporation that collects a half-cent sales tax off goods purchased in the city of Pflugerville for the purpose of promoting economic development.\nThe PCDC was founded in August 2001 with the mission of making Pflugerville a regional employment center by supporting business retention, expansion and attraction; creating quality local jobs; and giving residents more opportunities to work close to home, according to the PCDC website.\nWhat they’re saying \nPCDC Executive Director Jerry Jones said the anniversary is about honoring the people, partnerships and vision that have helped shape Pflugerville’s economic story.\n“We are proud of the foundation built over the past 25 years, and even more excited about what comes next as we continue creating opportunities, strengthening our business community, and building a prosperous future for Pflugerville,” Jones said.\nPCDC Marketing Manager Adam Maxon said one way the organization is supporting local entrepreneurs and small businesses is through Venture Pfest. Taking place Sept. 26-Oct. 1, the free week-long event will include workshops, panels, networking opportunities and resources.\nSeptember 11, 2026 \nDevelopment Pflugerville - Hutto \nData center, 7 Brew: Check out 5 major Austin-area permits filed this week\nSeptember 8, 2026 \n2d ago \nBusiness Pflugerville - Hutto \nDoll House Beauty Lounge now open in Hutto\n2d ago \n1d ago \nBusiness Bastrop - Cedar Creek \nDick’s Sporting Goods teased for Bastrop\n2d ago",
