    "content_text": "Evaluating AI and Machine Learning Approaches in Paint Formulation from an Industrial Raw Materials Perspective\nTurkchem \n19 Aug 2026 \n459 \n2 dk okuma \nThe bond issuance of Eker Süt Ürünleri, carried out through ÜNLÜ Menkul Değerler A.Ş., was completed with a nominal amount of TRY 350 million in line with the intense demand from investors. The transaction, which marks the company's first capital market instrument issuance in 2026, exceeded the initially planned amount.\nEker S&uuml;t &Uuml;r&uuml;nleri&rsquo;s bond issue, arranged through &Uuml;NL&Uuml; Menkul Değerler A.Ş., was completed at a nominal value of TRY 350 million on the back of strong investor demand. The transaction, the company&rsquo;s first capital markets instrument issue of 2026, exceeded the amount originally planned. \n&Uuml;NL&Uuml; Menkul Değerler A.Ş., a subsidiary of &Uuml;NL&Uuml; & Co, one of T&uuml;rkiye&rsquo;s investment services and asset management institutions, acted as intermediary for Eker S&uuml;t &Uuml;r&uuml;nleri&rsquo;s bond issue. Following the book-building process completed on 11 August 2026, the issue was carried out domestically through sale to qualified investors with a maturity of 372 days.\nInitially planned at a nominal value of TRY 300 million, the issue was raised to TRY 350 million in response to investor demand.\nDemand exceeded the planned issue size\nThe transaction, Eker S&uuml;t &Uuml;r&uuml;nleri&rsquo;s first capital markets instrument issue of 2026, was completed above the targeted amount thanks to investor demand.\nThe issue was among the transactions indicating that investor interest in the debt instruments of real sector companies is continuing.\n&ldquo;Interest in real sector debt instruments continues&rdquo; \nIn his assessment of the transaction, Tun&ccedil; Yıldırım, Managing Director of Corporate Sales at &Uuml;NL&Uuml; & Co, said qualified investors were maintaining their interest in the debt instruments of real sector companies.\nNoting that the size of the issue had been raised from TRY 300 million to TRY 350 million because of investor demand, Yıldırım said &Uuml;NL&Uuml; & Co continued to offer solutions for companies&rsquo; financing needs through its experience in capital markets and its institutional investor network.\nCapital markets continue to be an alternative source of finance \n&Ouml;zlem &Ccedil;elen, Director of Corporate & Treasury Solutions at &Uuml;NL&Uuml; Menkul Değerler A.Ş., emphasised that capital markets are becoming an increasingly important alternative source of finance for companies.\nNoting that the completion of Eker S&uuml;t &Uuml;r&uuml;nleri&rsquo;s first capital markets instrument issue above the planned amount demonstrated investor interest, &Ccedil;elen said that as &Uuml;NL&Uuml; Menkul Değerler they would continue to support companies&rsquo; access to capital markets.\n&nbsp;\nAbout &Uuml;NL&Uuml; & Co \nFounded in Istanbul in 1996, &Uuml;NL&Uuml; & Co is a financial services group operating in investment services and asset management. Present in five different regions of T&uuml;rkiye and, internationally, in the United Kingdom and the United States, the group serves individual and institutional investors through its &Uuml;NL&Uuml; Menkul Değerler, &Uuml;NL&Uuml; Portf&ouml;y, İstanbul Varlık, DAHA Yatırım Danışmanlığı and Piapiri brands.\nThe company has completed 139 mergers and acquisitions advisory transactions to date with a total value of approximately USD 20 billion. It also ranks among T&uuml;rkiye&rsquo;s leading financial institutions by transaction volume in public offerings and capital markets deals.\nGallery\n# EKONOMİ # Ürünleri # Tahvil # Hracı \nShare this story \nAdvertisement Ad Space 728 × 90",
