    "content_text": "Ouster's LiDAR Shipments Jump 70% Y/Y in Q2: Will Demand Sustain?\nZacks Equity Research \nAugust 17, 2026 3 min read \nOUST \n+0.29% \nOuster, Inc. OUST continued to focus on strategic execution and expansion, launching Rev8 in the second quarter of 2026, the world's first native color LiDAR sensor. Rev8 establishes a new benchmark in 3D spatial perception. Designed for functional safety and large-scale deployment, Rev8 is gaining traction across Ouster's key markets, including mining, construction, robotaxis and transportation infrastructure.&nbsp;\nCustomer adoption was reflected in several orders exceeding $1 million, including from the world's largest heavy machinery manufacturer, a leading autonomous agriculture equipment developer and a major autonomous vehicle provider. Ouster also secured a significant contract with the Utah Department of Transportation for its largest LiDAR deployment to date, covering several hundred intersections across the state.\nThe company also introduced advanced BlueCity detection powered by the Rev8 OS1Max, offering twice the range and resolution of previous generations and multimodal detection and classification capabilities of up to 500 feet. Advanced BlueCity detection could expand the types of roads and traffic environments where Ouster's LiDAR can be deployed, increasing the company's addressable market and potentially driving larger deployments.\nOuster is also expanding its LiDAR production capacity to support rising demand. The company expects unit volume growth to continue as adoption of physical AI accelerates. Its production run rate is expected to increase from about 40,000 units annually toward 100,000 units, with further capacity expansion likely to ensure sufficient headroom for customer demand and last-minute product SKU changes. OUST currently carries a Zacks Rank #4 (Sell).\nYou can see the complete list of today's Zacks #1 Rank (Strong Buy) stocks here . \nGrowth Trajectory of OUST's Competitors \nAeva Technologies, Inc. AEVA is positioned to benefit as LiDAR expands into higher-level ADAS and autonomy applications. In the second quarter of 2026, the company continued Atlas Ultra deliveries and integration for a top-10 European passenger OEM and advanced engagements with additional passenger and commercial OEMs. Bendix also selected Aeva's 4D LiDAR and perception software for its next-generation Level 2+ commercial-vehicle ADAS system.&nbsp;\nInnoviz Technologies Ltd. INVZ is expanding into defense and homeland security, where it sees significant long-term growth potential. Its automotive-grade LiDAR sensors are being adopted for applications including counter-UAS and perimeter protection. Through its new Perciz defense and security brand, Innoviz has secured six collaborations in three months. On July 30, the company received its first multimillion-dollar defense orders, totaling approximately $3.5 million. \nStory Continues \nOuster's Price Performance, Valuation and Estimates \nShares of Ouster have surged nearly 162% in the last six months. \nZacks Investment Research Image Source: Zacks Investment Research \nFrom a valuation standpoint, OUST trades at a forward price-to-sales ratio above 12.91x. \nZacks Investment Research Image Source: Zacks Investment Research \nThe Zacks Consensus Estimate for OUST's 2026 and 2027 loss per share has widened 4 cents and narrowed 28 cents, respectively, in the past 30 days. \nZacks Investment Research Image Source: Zacks Investment Research \nWant the latest recommendations from Zacks Investment Research? Today, you can download 7 Best Stocks for the Next 30 Days. Click to get this free report \nOuster, Inc. (OUST) : Free Stock Analysis Report \nAeva Technologies, Inc. (AEVA) : Free Stock Analysis Report \nInnoviz Technologies Ltd. (INVZ) : Free Stock Analysis Report \nThis article originally published on Zacks Investment Research (zacks.com). \nZacks Investment Research \nView Comments \nTerms and Privacy Policy