    "content_text": "Why Cognex Corporation (CGNX) Stock Is Down Today\nBy: Quiver PriceTracker\nPosted: 1 month, 1 week ago / Aug. 12, 2026 6:38 p.m. UTC \nCGNX\nCognex Corporation (CGNX) is down 3.2% today. Here is some analysis on what might have caused this price movement.\nAnalysis: The most likely explanation is a valuation-driven pullback rather than a new company-specific shock. Cognex had entered the session after a strong run, and investors may be taking profits even though the company’s most recent operating results and near-term outlook were solid. This could also be because the stock had climbed well above earlier analyst target levels, leaving less room for upside in the short term.\nDetails: Cognex’s latest reported quarter showed strong year-over-year growth in revenue, earnings, and adjusted profitability, which had helped lift sentiment earlier.\nManagement’s second-quarter 2026 guidance called for revenue of $280 million to $300 million and adjusted diluted earnings per share of $0.40 to $0.44, reinforcing expectations for continued growth.\nThe stock closed near $60.78 on August 12, 2026 after trading as high as $64.40 intraday, a sharp reversal that fits a profit-taking pattern more than a fundamental reset.\nA recent analyst target increase still noted that much of the good news appeared to be priced in, which may have encouraged investors to lock in gains after the rally.\nSources: \nCognex Investor Relations, SEC, Investing.com\nDisclaimer: This price movement analysis was generated with the help of AI. Please double-check the information provided for mistakes.\n$CGNX Insider Trading Activity\n$CGNX insiders have traded $CGNX stock on the open market 16 times in the past 6 months. Of those trades, 0 have been purchases and 16 have been sales .\nHere’s a breakdown of recent trading of $CGNX stock by insiders over the last 6 months:\nROBERT WILLETT has made 0 purchases and 3 sales selling 179,200 shares for an estimated $10,465,007 .\nJOERG KUECHEN (Head of Corporate M&A) has made 0 purchases and 4 sales selling 61,900 shares for an estimated $3,468,385 .\nDARREN MARC LONG (Vice President) has made 0 purchases and 4 sales selling 20,252 shares for an estimated $1,343,456 .\nLAURA ANN MACDONALD (VP and PAO) has made 0 purchases and 2 sales selling 14,881 shares for an estimated $850,553 .\nCARL GERST (EVP, Global Sales and Products) has made 0 purchases and 2 sales selling 14,336 shares for an estimated $802,021 .\nANGELOS PAPADIMITRIOU sold 4,150 shares for an estimated $230,658 \nTo track insider transactions, check out Quiver Quantitative's insider trading dashboard. You can access data on insider stock transactions through the Quiver Quantitative API insider transaction endpoint. \nEARLY ACCESS\nReceive CGNX Data Alerts\nReal-time alerts on filings, insider trades, and market signals — before everyone else.\nGet Alerts →\n$CGNX Hedge Fund Activity\nWe have seen 361 institutional investors add shares of $CGNX stock to their portfolio, and 261 decrease their positions in their most recent quarter.\nHere are some of the largest recent moves:\nNORTHWESTERN MUTUAL WEALTH MANAGEMENT CO removed 10,451,742 shares (-99.8%) from their portfolio in Q1 2026, for an estimated $512,030,840 \nMACKENZIE FINANCIAL CORP removed 1,817,037 shares (-69.5%) from their portfolio in Q1 2026, for an estimated $89,016,642 \nPOINT72 ASSET MANAGEMENT, L.P. removed 1,580,967 shares (-42.6%) from their portfolio in Q1 2026, for an estimated $77,451,573 \nARROWSTREET CAPITAL, LIMITED PARTNERSHIP added 1,090,092 shares (+115.6%) to their portfolio in Q1 2026, for an estimated $53,403,607 \nMUNRO PARTNERS added 1,046,750 shares (+inf%) to their portfolio in Q2 2026, for an estimated $75,805,635 \nPICTET ASSET MANAGEMENT HOLDING SA removed 843,153 shares (-12.6%) from their portfolio in Q2 2026, for an estimated $61,061,140 \nSUMITOMO MITSUI TRUST GROUP, INC. added 805,210 shares (+57.1%) to their portfolio in Q2 2026, for an estimated $58,313,308 \nTo track hedge funds' stock portfolios, check out Quiver Quantitative's institutional holdings dashboard. You can access data on hedge funds moves and 13F filings through the Quiver Quantitative API 13F endpoint. \n$CGNX Analyst Ratings\nWall Street analysts have issued reports on $CGNX in the last several months. We have seen 1 firms issue buy ratings on the stock, and 0 firms issue sell ratings.\nHere are some recent analyst ratings:\nNeedham issued a \"Buy\" rating on 05/08/2026\nTo track analyst ratings and price targets for $CGNX, check out Quiver Quantitative's $CGNX forecast page. \n$CGNX Price Targets\nMultiple analysts have issued price targets for $CGNX recently. We have seen 9 analysts offer price targets for $CGNX in the last 6 months, with a median target of $75.0.\nHere are some recent targets:\nJamie Cook from Truist Securities set a target price of $71.0 on 07/02/2026\nTomohiko Sano from JP Morgan set a target price of $75.0 on 05/26/2026\nMatthew Summerville from DA Davidson set a target price of $62.0 on 05/14/2026\nGuy Hardwick from Barclays set a target price of $75.0 on 05/11/2026\nJoe Ritchie from Goldman Sachs set a target price of $80.0 on 05/11/2026\nJames Ricchiuti from Needham set a target price of $75.0 on 05/08/2026\nPiyush Avasthy from Citigroup set a target price of $68.0 on 05/08/2026\nThis article is not financial advice. See Quiver Quantitative's disclaimers for more information. Note that there may be inaccuracies due to mistakes in ticker-mapping, and other anomalies. \nAdd Quiver Quantitative to your preferred sources on Google\nSuggested Articles \nTrump Announces U.S. Agreement for Permanent Security Control in Greenland \nSept. 18, 2026 9:38 p.m. UTC \nTrump Says CNN, MS NOW and Politico Banned From White House \nSept. 18, 2026 7:37 p.m. UTC \nPelosi’s Bloom Energy Options Gain an Estimated $1.5 Million \nSept. 17, 2026 5:19 p.m. UTC",
